which work as they do on the context.

Its fields are:

=over

=item account_sid

The SID of the L<Account|https://www.twilio.com/docs/api/rest/account> that
created the Service resource.

=item consumption_report_interval

DEPRECATED. The interval in seconds between consumption reports submission
batches from client endpoints.

=item date_created

The date and time in GMT when the resource was created specified in L<RFC
2822|http://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc2822.txt> format. A L<Time::Piece> object in
UTC. See L<Twilio::Deserialize/date_time>.

=item date_updated

The date and time in GMT when the resource was last updated specified in L<RFC
2822|http://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc2822.txt> format. A L<Time::Piece> object in
UTC. See L<Twilio::Deserialize/date_time>.

=item default_channel_creator_role_sid

The channel role assigned to a channel creator when they join a new channel.
See the L<Roles endpoint|https://www.twilio.com/docs/chat/api/roles> for more
details.

=item default_channel_role_sid

The channel role assigned to users when they are added to a channel. See the
L<Roles endpoint|https://www.twilio.com/docs/chat/api/roles> for more details.

=item default_service_role_sid

The service role assigned to users when they are added to the service. See the
L<Roles endpoint|https://www.twilio.com/docs/chat/api/roles> for more details.

=item friendly_name

The string that you assigned to describe the resource.

=item limits

An object that describes the limits of the service instance. The C<limits>
object contains C<channel_members> to describe the members/channel limit and
C<user_channels> to describe the channels/user limit. C<channel_members> can be
1,000 or less, with a default of 250. C<user_channels> can be 1,000 or less,
with a default value of 100.

=item links

The absolute URLs of the Service's
L<Channels|https://www.twilio.com/docs/chat/api/channels>,
L<Roles|https://www.twilio.com/docs/chat/api/roles>, and
L<Users|https://www.twilio.com/docs/chat/api/users>.

=item notifications

The notification configuration for the Service instance. See L<Push
Notification
Configuration|https://www.twilio.com/docs/chat/push-notification-configuration>
for more information.

=item post_webhook_url

The URL for post-event webhooks, which are called by using the
C<webhook_method>. See L<Webhook
Events|https://www.twilio.com/docs/api/chat/webhooks> for more details.

=item pre_webhook_url

The URL for pre-event webhooks, which are called by using the
C<webhook_method>. See L<Webhook
Events|https://www.twilio.com/docs/api/chat/webhooks> for more details.

=item reachability_enabled

Whether the L<Reachability
Indicator|https://www.twilio.com/docs/chat/reachability-indicator> is enabled
for this Service instance. The default is C<false>.

=item read_status_enabled

Whether the L<Message Consumption
Horizon|https://www.twilio.com/docs/chat/consumption-horizon> feature is
enabled. The default is C<true>.

=item sid

The unique string that we created to identify the Service resource.

=item typing_indicator_timeout

How long in seconds after a C<started typing> event until clients should assume
that user is no longer typing, even if no C<ended typing> message was received.
The default is 5 seconds.

=item url

The absolute URL of the Service resource.

=item webhook_filters

The list of WebHook events that are enabled for this Service instance. See
L<Webhook Events|https://www.twilio.com/docs/chat/webhook-events> for more
details.

=item webhook_method

The HTTP method to use for calls to the C<pre_webhook_url> and
C<post_webhook_url> webhooks. Can be: C<POST> or C<GET> and the default is
C<POST>. See L<Webhook Events|https://www.twilio.com/docs/chat/webhook-events>
for more details.

=item webhooks

An object that contains information about the webhooks configured for this
service.

=back

=head1 CONSTRUCTORS

=head2 new

Objects here come from the methods above, so there is no need to call C<new>
directly.

